                        class="text-[length:var(--fs-h2)] md:text-[length:var(--fs-h1)] leading-[length:var(--lh-h2)] md:leading-[length:var(--lh-h1)] font-medium text-text-default max-w-150 mb-4 md:mb-6"
                    >
                        Ireland e-invoicing at a glance
                    </h2>
                    <p
                        class="text-neutral-500 font-normal text-[length:var(--fs-body-lg)] leading-[length:var(--lh-body-lg)] max-w-151"
                    >
                        From 1 November 2028, large corporates must issue
                        structured e-invoices for domestic B2B sales and report
                        invoice data to Revenue in near real time. From the same
                        day, every VAT-registered business in Ireland must be
                        able to receive them. The obligation extends to
                        Ireland’s domestic B2B invoicing and reporting
                        requirements for VAT-registered businesses engaged in
                        qualifying cross-border EU B2B trade.
                    </p>
